_id":"U_kgDOBhBukQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101740177?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MWRAlves","html_url":"https://github.com/MWRAlves","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MWRAlves/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MWRAlves/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MWRAlves/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MWRAlves/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MWRAlves/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MWRAlves/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MWRAlves/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MWRAlves/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MWRAlves/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T13:40:11Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T13:40:11Z","body":"Oops, we weren't aware someone else had already attempted to implement the algorithm. Still, hopefully our code can be useful for something else. We're still students learning how to contribute to open source for the first time.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4670849790/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4671214708","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120145#issuecomment-4671214708","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120145","id":4671214708,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFm0UdA","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-10T14:18:48Z","updated_at":"2026-06-10T14:18:48Z","body":"I would ask that a simple test project is added to this PR so testers don't have to do the involved navigation setup manually. It is simple enough to do for someone familiar with the navigation system but a generic tester might often not even know where to start or create a polygon situation to test the difference in path and quality.\r\n\r\n> We weren't aware someone else had already attempted to implement the algorithm.\r\n\r\nDon't worry as the existence of the linked Dijkstra PR is irrelevant for this PR here as outside the same name and core algo they have nothing to do with each other.\r\n\r\nThe linked PR attempts to add a standalone similar to AStar3D which is all point-based, not polygon-based. It also does not touch or integrate with the navigation system and api, The AStar2D/3D classes all exist in an isolated \"math\" engine part because they are not necessarily used for actual gameplay pathfinding but for generic point graph searches. Also why they are over-watched by the core team and not the navigation team.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4671214708/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confu